<h2>Why we focus on appraisal</h2>
<p>Most claim professionals do a little of everything. Indiana Insurance Appraiser works on one question, the amount of loss, and we built our process, documentation and tools around answering it well. That focus lets us serve as your named appraiser, review an estimate before a dispute escalates, or sit as a neutral umpire on panels where we represent neither side.</p>
<h2>How we work</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Scope first.</strong> We inspect and measure before we look at anyone else’s numbers.</li>
<li><strong>Defensible, not inflated.</strong> An inflated estimate loses credibility with an umpire. We price what we can support.</li>
<li><strong>Plain English.</strong> You’ll understand every difference between our valuation and the carrier’s.</li>
<li><strong>Honest triage.</strong> If your claim needs an attorney or a public adjuster instead, we say so.</li>
<li><strong>Fees in writing</strong> before any work starts.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Who we work with</h2>
<p>Homeowners, condo owners, landlords, farm families, HOA boards, property managers, churches, business owners, contractors, public adjusters and attorneys across Indiana. On any claim we serve in one role only, and we disclose any prior relationship with the other appraiser or the umpire.</p>
<h2>What we are not</h2>
<p>We aren’t a law firm and don’t give legal advice. We don’t act as public adjusters or negotiate claims outside the appraisal process. We don’t guarantee outcomes, and no honest appraiser can.</p>
<h2>Statewide, by design</h2>
<p>Indiana’s weather changes from one end of the state to the other: lake-effect snow in South Bend, hail in Carmel, derechos across the Wabash Valley, ice storms and tornadoes along the Ohio River. Working all 92 counties means we see every kind of loss the state produces and price each one with local knowledge.</p></article><aside class="sidebar"><div class="sticky"><div class="side-box call-box"><p class="side-h">Talk it through</p><p>A free first conversation. We’ll tell you honestly whether appraisal fits your claim.</p><a class="call-num" href="tel:+18445371427">+1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-gold btn-block" href="/contact-us/">Send claim details</a></div><div class="side-box"><p class="side-h">Explore</p><ul class="side-list"><li><a href="/indiana-claim-appraisal/">Our services</a></li><li><a href="/hoosier-cities/">Indiana cities</a></li><li><a href="/claim-gap-tools/">Free tools</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-process-indiana/">Appraisal process</a></li></ul></div></div></aside></div><section class="cta-band"><div class="checker thin" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="wrap cta-in rv"><div><h2>Is the carrier’s number short?</h2><p>Send us the estimate. We’ll read it line by line and tell you what we see.</p></div><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-gold" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line light" href="/contact-us/">Email the estimate</a></div></div></section>
